Let \(0<\epsilon\le1\), \(u>0\), \(p\ge0\), and \(w\ge0\), and let \(q_0,q_1\in[0,p]\).  For \(a\in\{0,1\}\), let \(\lambda_a\) satisfy \(\epsilon w\le\lambda_a\le w\), and let \(r_{2,a},r_{4,a}\ge0\) satisfy \((1+\lambda_a)^2r_{2,a}\le8\) and \((1+\lambda_a)^4r_{4,a}\le96\).  Put \(c_{\mathrm{mar}}=8\epsilon^{-2}+96(\epsilon^{-2}+\epsilon^{-3})\).  Then
\[
\lambda_1\bigl\{(q_1u^{-1}+q_1^2)(\lambda_0+\lambda_0^2)r_{4,1}+(q_0u^{-1}+q_0^2)r_{2,0}\bigr\}
+\lambda_0\bigl\{(q_0u^{-1}+q_0^2)(\lambda_1+\lambda_1^2)r_{4,0}+(q_1u^{-1}+q_1^2)r_{2,1}\bigr\}
\le (pu^{-1}+p^2)\,\frac{2c_{\mathrm{mar}}}{1+w}.
\]
